# Extrapolate the Impossible: "You may reveal exactly two cards you own with different names from outside the game. An
# opponent chooses one of them. You put that card into your hand." Bot1's sideboard holds Lightning Bolt and Counterspell
# (CR 400.11a: a sideboard is outside the game), so both are offered. Bot1 reveals the pair and Bot2 - the opponent -
# names Counterspell, which Bot1 puts into their hand (CR 400.11b); the Bolt stays outside the game, where the spell left
# it (CR 701.20b, 400.11c), so the sideboard holds it still. Bot2's Shock is outside the game too, but it is not a card
# Bot1 owns, so it is not among those Bot1 may reveal (CR 108.3b, 400.11a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Extrapolate the Impossible
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Island
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot2 Sideboard]
Shock

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Extrapolate the Impossible.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
? Stack.Count = 1
! Bot1.Choose(Shock)
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Choose(Counterspell)
Bot2.Choose(Counterspell)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Counterspell; Swamp; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Sideboard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Extrapolate the Impossible
Bot2.Sideboard = Shock
Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
Stack.Count = 0
